WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.509
Please welcome today's Drew-Gooder, Joe Caramagna.

2
00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:04.823
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

3
00:00:04.823 --> 00:00:05.717
Thank you.

4
00:00:07.669 --> 00:00:09.080
Okay, I hear you're known

5
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.730
for being like a doughnut connoisseur.

6
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.481
I can't even believe this is in front of me right now.

7
00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:14.350
(Joe laughs)
(audience laughs)

8
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:17.620
Yeah, I have a little bit of a reputation, I guess.

9
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.200
I make comic books and graphic novels for a living.

10
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.770
So I travel to a lot of different comic conventions

11
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.050
across the country.

12
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.260
And the joke is that I tell people to bring me doughnuts

13
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.890
or other sweet treats and I'll pay them back in comics,

14
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.150
and people do.

15
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.069
They bring me doughnuts all the time.

16
00:00:33.069 --> 00:00:33.902
(audience laughs)

17
00:00:33.902 --> 00:00:36.240
And everywhere I travel, I always,

18
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.730
I seek out the local doughnut shop, and I sample it

19
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.580
and test them out and everything.

20
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.480 line:15%
And I end up keeping in touch

21
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.520 line:15%
with a lot of the shops on social media.

22
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.460 line:15%
And one of the shops is Broad Street Dough Co.,

23
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.680 line:15%
which is in Oakhurst, New Jersey.

24
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.230
They also have a store in Freehold.

25
00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.150
And they actually gave me the opportunity

26
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.139
to create my own doughnut that I call the Joenut. (laughs)

27
00:00:58.139 --> 00:00:59.106
The Joenut!
(audience applauds)

28
00:00:59.106 --> 00:01:00.886
Yeah.
That's so perfect!

29
00:01:00.886 --> 00:01:02.403
(Joe laughs)

30
00:01:02.403 --> 00:01:04.990
How did you start matriculating

31
00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:09.070
and associating doughnuts with like philanthropy?

32
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.620
How did that happen?

33
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.090
Well, pre-pandemic, I used to raise money

34
00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.450
for the Ronald McDonald House Charities

35
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.240
at different comic conventions.

36
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.940
And I would put a little change box

37
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.930
in front of me at the meet-and-greet table,

38
00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.660
and people would come by and draw up in like $5, $10,

39
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.360
and I would give them signed comics in return.

40
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.140
But unfortunately, because of the pandemic,

41
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.250
a lot of live events kinda went away for a while.

42
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.310
And Krispy Kreme announced their promotion

43
00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:36.110
that they would give away one free glazed doughnut

44
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.790
every day if you show your vaccination card.

45
00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.623
That's right.

46
00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:40.855
We did a story about that on the news,

47
00:01:40.855 --> 00:01:41.688
yeah.
Right.

48
00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:43.400
And I take a walk every morning

49
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.970
as part of my just daily routine.

50
00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.450
So there's a store that happens to be a mile away

51
00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.283
from my house.

52
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:51.660
So I turn that into my daily walk

53
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.260
and started going every day.

54
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.950
And (laughs) I would post pictures of me

55
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.810
with my free doughnut on social media,

56
00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.350
and put a little silly caption or something,

57
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.980
and try to encourage people to get vaccinated.

58
00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.910
And people seem to enjoy it.

59
00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:10.880
And I decided that I would do something

60
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.840
and kinda tie in my love

61
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.550
for the Ronald McDonald House Charities,

62
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:17.390
and I decided to give $1 for every free doughnut I got.

63
00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.240
The money I'm saving on doughnuts,

64
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.600
I'll donate to the Ronald McDonald House

65
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.400
in Winston-Salem, North Carolina.

66
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.770
And this is personal for you, the Ronald McDonald House.

67
00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.020
Will you tell us why?

68
00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.180
Sure.

69
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.090
When my oldest daughter, Julia, was born,

70
00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.630
she had some life-threatening complications,

71
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.950
and she had to be transported to another hospital,

72
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.000
a children's hospital.

73
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.550
And that's pretty much where my wife

74
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.733
and I lived for the first month of her life.

75
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.270
But I remember feeling very lucky, actually, because my wife

76
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.750
and I actually lived somewhat close to the hospital,

77
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.120
so we were able to go back and forth to home.

78
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.880
And we saw some families there

79
00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.690
that didn't have that situation,

80
00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.760
and they had to sleep in waiting rooms

81
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.820
and pushing like two chairs together to make a bed.

82
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.210
And years later, I found out what it is

83
00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.610 line:15%
that the Ronald McDonald House actually does.

84
00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.660 line:15%
And that's provide a home away from home

85
00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.080 line:15%
for families with seriously ill children

86
00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.060
that have to travel a long distance to go to the hospital.

87
00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.550
And as soon as I found that out,

88
00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.603
I knew that that's a mission that I wanted to be a part of

89
00:03:19.603 --> 00:03:22.671
because I actually saw the need for it.

90
00:03:22.671 --> 00:03:23.880
Oh, you're so...

91
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.520
I love this so much. You're such a good person.

92
00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.353
I'm-

93
00:03:27.353 --> 00:03:28.186
Thank you.
(audience applauds)

94
00:03:28.186 --> 00:03:29.843
So glad that you're doing this.

95
00:03:29.843 --> 00:03:31.001
Thank you.

96
00:03:31.001 --> 00:03:34.267
I'm sorry that you had to go through that

97
00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:37.560
and so grateful that you were able to turn your pain

98
00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.330
and fear into this awareness and take care of others.

99
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:43.760
Our friends at The Make Sense Foundation,

100
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.540
founded by SeneGence, a female-owned cosmetic brand,

101
00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.950
heard what you were doing and they wanted to help.

102
00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.350
So they're donating $10,000

103
00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.340
to the Ronald McDonald House
(audience cheers)

104
00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.378
of the Piedmont Triad
(audience cheers)

105
00:03:57.378 --> 00:03:59.550
in your honor, Joe.

106
00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:00.720
Wow, thank you so much.

107
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.410
That's amazing. Thank you.

108
00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.530
There's also, we know that you've walked

109
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.340
over 400 miles for a good cause,

110
00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.650
and we wanted to give you something to keep you on your feet

111
00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.730
so you could keep doing all the good things you're doing.

112
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.390
And truMedic is gonna give you a massage chair.

113
00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.231
Oh, my gosh.
Believe me,

114
00:04:16.231 --> 00:04:17.064
(audience applauds)
(Joe laughs)

115
00:04:17.064 --> 00:04:18.636
we have one upstairs,

116
00:04:18.636 --> 00:04:20.870
and the entire crew uses it.
Wow.

117
00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.200
We all take turns.

118
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.270
Oh, wow.

119
00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:26.140
So maybe you can kick back, eat a doughnut,

120
00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:29.320
and realize that there are thousands and thousands

121
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.510
and thousands of dollars going to Ronald McDonald House

122
00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:32.343
in your honor.
Thank you so much.

123
00:04:32.343 --> 00:04:33.176
That's very kind.

124
00:04:33.176 --> 00:04:34.009
I'm gonna have to fight my kids

125
00:04:34.009 --> 00:04:35.247
for use of that massage chair.
(audience applauds)

126
00:04:35.247 --> 00:04:36.410
(Joe laughs)

127
00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.380 line:15%
If you saw us here, we're all fighting each other for it.

128
00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.213 line:15%
(Joe laughs)

129
00:04:39.213 --> 00:04:41.450 line:15%
It works like a charm.

130
00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.430 line:15%
Joe, thank you for doing what you're doing

131
00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:46.840 line:15%
and bringing awareness to the Ronald McDonald House,

132
00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.380
really and truly.

133
00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.430
Thank you so much for giving me the opportunity

134
00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.263
to talk about it.

135
00:04:51.263 --> 00:04:52.096
'Cause the first time I ever heard

136
00:04:52.096 --> 00:04:54.340
about the Ronald McDonald House was on a radio show,

137
00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:57.700
so I know how this can lead to good things,

138
00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.160
just putting it out there for people to see.

139
00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.250
Let's hope that it does.

140
00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.083
Let's try.
I hope so.

141
00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:03.850 line:15%
If you go to thedrewbarrymoreshow.com,

142
00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.210 line:15%
you'll learn all about how to donate

143
00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.590 line:15%
to the Ronald McDonald House and support that.

144
00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.605
And thank you, Joe.

145
00:05:09.605 --> 00:05:12.522 line:15%
(upbeat pop music)

